Lets the core say which of a tab's session history entries it may be taken to. Every traversal
starts in the five-argument NavigationControllerImpl::GoToIndex in
content/browser/renderer_host/navigation_controller_impl.cc: GoBack, GoForward, GoToIndex and
GoToOffset from the browser, GoToOffsetFromRenderer for a page's history.back(), forward() and
go(), and NavigateToNavigationApiKey for the Navigation API's back(), forward() and traverseTo(),
which asks no delegate on its way. A NavigationThrottle sees none of the traversals within one
document. So the filter content::SetHistoryTraversalFilter gives is asked there, with the entry's
index, before anything of the traversal starts; its false leaves the tab on its page, and a
Navigation API caller hears TraverseCancelled, as for a key no entry has. A hook only: a tab given
no filter pays one null check, and which entries a tab may be taken to is the core's.

